    description: "The booking date is chosen in a popover calendar. The trigger is a `<button>` labelled “Booking date” that shows “Choose a date” or the chosen day as DD/MM/YYYY; there is no input. The popover (`div role=dialog` “Choose the booking date”) shows whole Monday-first weeks as rows of `<button>`s, including the last days of the previous month and the first days of the next month, so numbers such as “1” appear twice. Days outside today + 2 … today + 60, the venue's weekly closed day (Kalaivani Nagar Community Hall: Tuesday) and fully booked days are natively `disabled`, with a `title` giving the reason. The window spans three calendar months, so later days need “Next month”. Choosing a day closes the popover and loads the slot map (OTH-21).",
    implementation: "BookingCalendar.tsx; window, closed days and the deterministic “booked by others” pattern are in booking.ts (`dayStatus`, `firstAvailableDay`, `calendarStart`, `monthNav`, `monthGrid`, `moveDay`). Day buttons have `aria-label` like “Saturday, 21 November 2026” (en-IN; Tamil in Tamil) and `aria-pressed` on the chosen day. One roving tab stop; opening focuses the chosen or first bookable day; arrows skip unavailable days, Home/End, PageUp/PageDown move, Enter/Space choose, Escape closes and refocuses the trigger; a mousedown outside closes it. The month buttons are natively `disabled` at the window's first/last month; when the focused one disables itself, focus moves to the other one, so Escape still works. Unlike DAT-06 the cells are real buttons and really disabled.",
    files: ["src/modules/bookings/BookingCalendar.tsx", "src/modules/bookings/booking.ts"],
