    description: "The booking is a `div[draggable=true][role=button]` card (booking number, date, time) above a week board: a plain `<table>` with one row per two-hour slot (row header “18:00 – 20:00”) and one column per day (“Thu 03/12”; closed days and days outside the window say so in the header). Taken cells say “Booked”, the booking's own cells “Your booking”, free cells are empty. Dragging the card onto a cell moves the booking to start at that cell's time on that day, keeping its length; during a real drag the cells it would cover are outlined. A drop on a booked slot, a closed day, a day outside the window or past closing time shows why (“03/12/2026, 10:00 – 14:00 is not free. Your booking has not been moved.”) and changes nothing. A good drop shows “Moving your booking…” (BOOKING_MOVE), then “Booking AMC/BK/… has been moved to 08/12/2026, 10:00 – 14:00.”, an SMS, and the row's new date and time. Previous week / Next week reload the board (BOOKING_WEEK). Keyboard: Space on the focused card picks it up, the arrow keys move a cursor (crossing weeks), Space moves the booking there, Escape cancels.",
