    files: ["src/modules/bookings/MoveBoard.tsx", "src/modules/bookings/manage.ts", "src/mock/endpoints/bookings.ts"],
    whyHard: "It is native HTML5 drag-and-drop: the drop handler needs a DragEvent whose DataTransfer carries the booking number. Measured in Chromium (Playwright 1.65): `dispatchEvent('dragstart')` / `dispatchEvent('drop')` without an init create a DragEvent with `dataTransfer === null`, so nothing moves; JS-dispatched `mousedown`/`mousemove`/`mouseup` never start a native drag; `locator.dragTo()` and `page.mouse.down()` → `hover()` → `up()` do run a real drag and move the booking; `dispatchEvent('drop', { dataTransfer })` with a `DataTransfer` holding the number as text/plain moves it without any drag. Selenium: WebDriver Actions `dragAndDrop` is widely reported not to start HTML5 drags in Chromium (unverified here: Selenium is not run in this repo). Target cells have no name of their own: find them through the row header (time) and the column position (day). Drops on taken cells are accepted by the board and refused afterwards, so a test that only checks for no error passes wrongly; the outcome must be read from the message, the table or the saved record.",
    selenium: "Use Actions first (`new Actions(driver).dragAndDrop(card, cell).perform()`); if the booking does not move, simulate the drop in JS: `js.executeScript(\"const dt=new DataTransfer();dt.setData('text/plain',arguments[2]);arguments[1].dispatchEvent(new DragEvent('drop',{bubbles:true,cancelable:true,dataTransfer:dt}))\", card, cell, \"AMC/BK/2026/004719\")`. The keyboard path also works: focus the card, `sendKeys(Keys.SPACE)`, arrows, `Keys.SPACE`. Not run with Selenium in this repo.",
    playwright: "`await card.dragTo(board.getByRole('row').filter({ has: page.getByRole('rowheader', { name: /^10:00 – / }) }).getByRole('cell').nth(dayIndex))`, then wait for “has been moved to …”. Without a real drag: `const dt = await page.evaluateHandle(r => { const d = new DataTransfer(); d.setData('text/plain', r); return d; }, ref); await cell.dispatchEvent('drop', { dataTransfer: dt })`.",
    assert: "The card is `draggable=true`; after `dragTo()` a free cell shows “Moving your booking…”, then the confirmation with that day and time, the cell says “Your booking”, the saved record has the same ref with the new date / slots / start / end / hours and the same amount, there is still one record, the table shows the new date and re-sorted order, also after a reload; `dispatchEvent` drag/drop without a DataTransfer and JS mouse events move nothing (and raise no page error), a drop with a DataTransfer carrying the number moves it; `page.mouse` drag moves it; a drop on a booked cell or a closed day shows the matching error, leaves “Your booking” where it was, saves nothing and shows no success; with BOOKING_MOVE failing only the error remains; a slot booked in the meantime is refused by the move and the board reloads; keyboard Space / arrows / Space moves it and Escape cancels; works with `{\"scale\":0}` and with today pinned to month ends (2026-12-31, 2027-01-30, 2027-02-27, 2028-02-28).",
